  user_input {
    user_response: "# Indian Multilingual Language Requirement\n\nThe platform must be designed as an **India-first real-time multilingual translation platform**.\n\nDo NOT restrict the architecture to English \342\206\222 Indian languages.\n\nThe system must support:\n\n**Indian language \342\206\222 Indian language**\n\n**English \342\206\222 Indian language**\n\n**Indian language \342\206\222 English**\n\n**Indian language \342\206\222 Indian language**\n\nThe source language and target language must be independently selectable.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nMarathi \342\206\222 Hindi\nHindi \342\206\222 Tamil\nTamil \342\206\222 Bengali\nBengali \342\206\222 Marathi\nGujarati \342\206\222 Telugu\nKannada \342\206\222 Malayalam\nPunjabi \342\206\222 Hindi\nOdia \342\206\222 Marathi\nAssamese \342\206\222 Bengali\nEnglish \342\206\222 Marathi\nMarathi \342\206\222 English\n```\n\nThe architecture must allow any supported source language to be translated into any supported target language.\n\n---\n\n# Initial Indian Language Set\n\nBuild the language architecture around the major languages of India, including:\n\n1. Hindi\n2. Bengali\n3. Marathi\n4. Telugu\n5. Tamil\n6. Gujarati\n7. Urdu\n8. Kannada\n9. Odia\n10. Malayalam\n11. Punjabi\n12. Assamese\n13. Maithili\n14. Sanskrit\n15. Konkani\n16. Nepali\n17. Sindhi\n18. Dogri\n19. Manipuri / Meitei\n20. Bodo\n21. Kashmiri\n22. Santali\n\nAlso support:\n\n23. English\n\nThe language system must be extensible so additional Indian languages and regional languages can be added without changing the core application architecture.\n\n---\n\n# Language Configuration\n\nDo NOT hardcode language behavior inside individual components.\n\nCreate a centralized language configuration.\n\nExample:\n\n```typescript\ninterface LanguageConfig {\n  code: string;\n  name: string;\n  nativeName: string;\n  script: string;\n  direction: \"ltr\" | \"rtl\";\n  sttSupported: boolean;\n  translationSupported: boolean;\n  ttsSupported: boolean;\n  enabled: boolean;\n}\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nHindi\nCode: hi\nNative Name: \340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\nScript: Devanagari\n\nMarathi\nCode: mr\nNative Name: \340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200\nScript: Devanagari\n\nBengali\nCode: bn\nNative Name: \340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\202\340\246\262\340\246\276\nScript: Bengali\n\nTamil\nCode: ta\nNative Name: \340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\nScript: Tamil\n```\n\n---\n\n# Language Selection\n\nThe listener should be able to search languages.\n\nDo not display 20+ languages as a huge list.\n\nUse:\n\n```text\nChoose your language\n\n\360\237\224\215 Search language...\n\nPopular\n\n\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\n\340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200\n\340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\202\340\246\262\340\246\276\n\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\340\260\244\340\261\206\340\260\262\340\261\201\340\260\227\340\261\201\n\340\252\227\340\253\201\340\252\234\340\252\260\340\252\276\340\252\244\340\253\200\n\nAll Indian Languages\n\nAssamese\nBengali\nBodo\nDogri\nGujarati\nHindi\nKannada\nKashmiri\nKonkani\nMaithili\nMalayalam\nManipuri\nMarathi\nNepali\nOdia\nPunjabi\nSanskrit\nSantali\nSindhi\nTamil\nTelugu\nUrdu\n```\n\nDisplay each language using both:\n\n**Native name + English name**\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\n\340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200\nMarathi\n```\n\nThis makes the platform usable by people who may not be comfortable reading English.\n\n---\n\n# Dynamic Translation Matrix\n\nThe architecture should support a dynamic translation matrix.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n                TARGET\n\n          Hindi Marathi Tamil Bengali\nSOURCE\nHindi       \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nMarathi     \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nTamil       \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nBengali     \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nGujarati    \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nKannada     \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\n...\n```\n\nDo not create separate hardcoded translation functions such as:\n\n```text\ntranslateEnglishToHindi()\ntranslateEnglishToMarathi()\ntranslateEnglishToTamil()\n```\n\nInstead create:\n\n```typescript\ntranslate(\n  sourceLanguage,\n  targetLanguage,\n  text\n)\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```typescript\ntranslate(\"mr\", \"ta\", text)\n```\n\nThis allows the platform to support any source \342\206\222 target combination.\n\n---\n\n# Real-Time Processing\n\nThe pipeline must become:\n\n```text\nSpeaker\n   \342\206\223\nMicrophone\n   \342\206\223\nSource Language Detection / Selected Source Language\n   \342\206\223\nReal-Time Speech-to-Text\n   \342\206\223\nSource Transcript\n   \342\206\223\nTranslation Router\n   \342\206\223\nTarget Language\n   \342\206\223\nTranslated Text\n   \342\206\223\nText-to-Speech\n   \342\206\223\nListener\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nSpeaker speaks Marathi\n\n\"\340\244\206\340\244\234 \340\244\206\340\244\252\340\244\243 \340\244\225\340\245\203\340\244\244\340\245\215\340\244\260\340\244\277\340\244\256 \340\244\254\340\245\201\340\244\246\340\245\215\340\244\247\340\244\277\340\244\256\340\244\244\340\245\215\340\244\244\340\245\207\340\244\254\340\244\246\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\244\262 \340\244\266\340\244\277\340\244\225\340\244\243\340\244\276\340\244\260 \340\244\206\340\244\271\340\245\213\340\244\244.\"\n\n        \342\206\223\n\nSTT\n\n        \342\206\223\n\nMarathi transcript\n\n        \342\206\223\n\nTranslation Router\n\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Hindi\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Tamil\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Bengali\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Gujarati\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Telugu\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 English\n\n        \342\206\223\n\nEach listener receives\ntheir selected language.\n```\n\n---\n\n# Important: Language Detection\n\nAllow the broadcaster to select the source language manually.\n\nAlso provide an optional:\n\n**Auto Detect Language**\n\nfeature.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nSource Language\n\n\342\227\213 Marathi\n\342\227\213 Hindi\n\342\227\213 English\n\342\227\217 Auto Detect\n```\n\nIf Auto Detect is enabled, the system should identify the spoken language where the underlying speech recognition provider supports reliable detection.\n\nManual selection should remain the recommended option for maximum accuracy.\n\n---\n\n# Indian Script Support\n\nThe UI must correctly render Indian scripts.\n\nTest the application with:\n\n```text\n\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\n\340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200\n\340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\202\340\246\262\340\246\276\n\340\252\227\340\253\201\340\252\234\340\252\260\340\252\276\340\252\244\340\253\200\n\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\340\260\244\340\261\206\340\260\262\340\261\201\340\260\227\340\261\201\n\340\262\225\340\262\250\340\263\215\340\262\250\340\262\241\n\340\264\256\340\264\262\340\264\257\340\264\276\340\264\263\340\264\202\n\340\254\223\340\254\241\340\254\274\340\254\277\340\254\206\n\340\250\252\340\251\260\340\250\234\340\250\276\340\250\254\340\251\200\n\340\246\205\340\246\270\340\246\256\340\247\200\340\246\257\340\246\274\340\246\276\n\330\247\330\261\330\257\331\210\n\340\244\270\340\244\202\340\244\270\340\245\215\340\244\225\340\245\203\340\244\244\n\340\244\250\340\245\207\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\245\200\n\340\244\256\340\245\210\340\244\245\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\245\200\n\340\244\225\340\245\213\340\244\202\340\244\225\340\244\243\340\245\200\n\330\263\331\206\332\214\331\212\n\340\244\241\340\245\213\340\244\227\340\244\260\340\245\200\n\340\244\270\340\244\202\340\244\245\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\245\200\n\340\244\254\340\245\213\340\244\241\340\245\213\n\340\246\256\340\247\210\340\246\244\340\247\210\340\246\262\340\247\213\340\246\250\340\247\215\n\332\251\331\262\330\264\331\217\330\261\n```\n\nUse Unicode throughout the system.\n\nDo not assume Latin/English characters.\n\n---\n\n# RTL Language Support\n\nThe platform must support languages such as Urdu and Sindhi that may require right-to-left rendering.\n\nThe interface should dynamically switch text direction based on the selected language.\n\nExample:\n\n```typescript\ndirection = language.direction\n```\n\nFor RTL languages:\n\n```text\ndir=\"rtl\"\n```\n\nEnsure transcript, translated text, controls and typography remain usable.\n\n---\n\n# Indian Language Audio\n\nText-to-speech must also be language-aware.\n\nThe system should select an appropriate voice based on:\n\n```text\nlanguage\n+\nregion\n+\navailable voice\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nHindi \342\206\222 Hindi voice\nMarathi \342\206\222 Marathi voice\nTamil \342\206\222 Tamil voice\nBengali \342\206\222 Bengali voice\nTelugu \342\206\222 Telugu voice\n```\n\nDo not simply use an English voice to pronounce Indian-language text.\n\n---\n\n# Language Quality Layer\n\nCreate a provider capability system.\n\nNot every AI provider will have equal quality for every Indian language.\n\nTherefore maintain:\n\n```typescript\ninterface LanguageCapability {\n  languageCode: string;\n  speechToText: boolean;\n  translation: boolean;\n  textToSpeech: boolean;\n  qualityLevel: \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"experimental\";\n}\n```\n\nThe platform should know which services support which languages.\n\nIf a language does not have reliable TTS, allow:\n\n**Text-only translation**\n\ninstead of breaking the entire experience.\n\n---\n\n# Future Expansion\n\nThe architecture must allow adding:\n\n* More Indian regional languages\n* Dialects\n* Indian English\n* Hinglish\n* Regional accents\n* Code-mixed speech\n\nFuture examples:\n\n```text\nHinglish \342\206\222 Marathi\nMarathi + English \342\206\222 Hindi\nTamil + English \342\206\222 Telugu\nHindi + English \342\206\222 Bengali\n```\n\nDo not build the initial architecture in a way that assumes users speak only one pure language.\n\n---\n\n# Core Product Principle\n\nThe platform should ultimately work like:\n\n**Speak in ANY supported Indian language \342\206\222 listener chooses ANY supported Indian language \342\206\222 translation happens live.**\n\nThe user should never need to know which AI model or translation provider is being used.\n\nThe complexity belongs inside the platform.\n\nThe user experience should remain:\n\n```text\nI SPEAK\n   \342\206\223\nCHOOSE MY LANGUAGE\n\nI LISTEN\n   \342\206\223\nCHOOSE MY LANGUAGE\n\nLIVE TRANSLATION\n```\n\nThe long-term goal is to make the platform a **real-time language bridge for India**.\n"
    items {
      text: "# Indian Multilingual Language Requirement\n\nThe platform must be designed as an **India-first real-time multilingual translation platform**.\n\nDo NOT restrict the architecture to English \342\206\222 Indian languages.\n\nThe system must support:\n\n**Indian language \342\206\222 Indian language**\n\n**English \342\206\222 Indian language**\n\n**Indian language \342\206\222 English**\n\n**Indian language \342\206\222 Indian language**\n\nThe source language and target language must be independently selectable.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nMarathi \342\206\222 Hindi\nHindi \342\206\222 Tamil\nTamil \342\206\222 Bengali\nBengali \342\206\222 Marathi\nGujarati \342\206\222 Telugu\nKannada \342\206\222 Malayalam\nPunjabi \342\206\222 Hindi\nOdia \342\206\222 Marathi\nAssamese \342\206\222 Bengali\nEnglish \342\206\222 Marathi\nMarathi \342\206\222 English\n```\n\nThe architecture must allow any supported source language to be translated into any supported target language.\n\n---\n\n# Initial Indian Language Set\n\nBuild the language architecture around the major languages of India, including:\n\n1. Hindi\n2. Bengali\n3. Marathi\n4. Telugu\n5. Tamil\n6. Gujarati\n7. Urdu\n8. Kannada\n9. Odia\n10. Malayalam\n11. Punjabi\n12. Assamese\n13. Maithili\n14. Sanskrit\n15. Konkani\n16. Nepali\n17. Sindhi\n18. Dogri\n19. Manipuri / Meitei\n20. Bodo\n21. Kashmiri\n22. Santali\n\nAlso support:\n\n23. English\n\nThe language system must be extensible so additional Indian languages and regional languages can be added without changing the core application architecture.\n\n---\n\n# Language Configuration\n\nDo NOT hardcode language behavior inside individual components.\n\nCreate a centralized language configuration.\n\nExample:\n\n```typescript\ninterface LanguageConfig {\n  code: string;\n  name: string;\n  nativeName: string;\n  script: string;\n  direction: \"ltr\" | \"rtl\";\n  sttSupported: boolean;\n  translationSupported: boolean;\n  ttsSupported: boolean;\n  enabled: boolean;\n}\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nHindi\nCode: hi\nNative Name: \340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\nScript: Devanagari\n\nMarathi\nCode: mr\nNative Name: \340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200\nScript: Devanagari\n\nBengali\nCode: bn\nNative Name: \340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\202\340\246\262\340\246\276\nScript: Bengali\n\nTamil\nCode: ta\nNative Name: \340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\nScript: Tamil\n```\n\n---\n\n# Language Selection\n\nThe listener should be able to search languages.\n\nDo not display 20+ languages as a huge list.\n\nUse:\n\n```text\nChoose your language\n\n\360\237\224\215 Search language...\n\nPopular\n\n\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\n\340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200\n\340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\202\340\246\262\340\246\276\n\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\340\260\244\340\261\206\340\260\262\340\261\201\340\260\227\340\261\201\n\340\252\227\340\253\201\340\252\234\340\252\260\340\252\276\340\252\244\340\253\200\n\nAll Indian Languages\n\nAssamese\nBengali\nBodo\nDogri\nGujarati\nHindi\nKannada\nKashmiri\nKonkani\nMaithili\nMalayalam\nManipuri\nMarathi\nNepali\nOdia\nPunjabi\nSanskrit\nSantali\nSindhi\nTamil\nTelugu\nUrdu\n```\n\nDisplay each language using both:\n\n**Native name + English name**\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\n\340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200\nMarathi\n```\n\nThis makes the platform usable by people who may not be comfortable reading English.\n\n---\n\n# Dynamic Translation Matrix\n\nThe architecture should support a dynamic translation matrix.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n                TARGET\n\n          Hindi Marathi Tamil Bengali\nSOURCE\nHindi       \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nMarathi     \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nTamil       \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nBengali     \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nGujarati    \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\nKannada     \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223      \342\234\223\n...\n```\n\nDo not create separate hardcoded translation functions such as:\n\n```text\ntranslateEnglishToHindi()\ntranslateEnglishToMarathi()\ntranslateEnglishToTamil()\n```\n\nInstead create:\n\n```typescript\ntranslate(\n  sourceLanguage,\n  targetLanguage,\n  text\n)\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```typescript\ntranslate(\"mr\", \"ta\", text)\n```\n\nThis allows the platform to support any source \342\206\222 target combination.\n\n---\n\n# Real-Time Processing\n\nThe pipeline must become:\n\n```text\nSpeaker\n   \342\206\223\nMicrophone\n   \342\206\223\nSource Language Detection / Selected Source Language\n   \342\206\223\nReal-Time Speech-to-Text\n   \342\206\223\nSource Transcript\n   \342\206\223\nTranslation Router\n   \342\206\223\nTarget Language\n   \342\206\223\nTranslated Text\n   \342\206\223\nText-to-Speech\n   \342\206\223\nListener\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nSpeaker speaks Marathi\n\n\"\340\244\206\340\244\234 \340\244\206\340\244\252\340\244\243 \340\244\225\340\245\203\340\244\244\340\245\215\340\244\260\340\244\277\340\244\256 \340\244\254\340\245\201\340\244\246\340\245\215\340\244\247\340\244\277\340\244\256\340\244\244\340\245\215\340\244\244\340\245\207\340\244\254\340\244\246\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\244\262 \340\244\266\340\244\277\340\244\225\340\244\243\340\244\276\340\244\260 \340\244\206\340\244\271\340\245\213\340\244\244.\"\n\n        \342\206\223\n\nSTT\n\n        \342\206\223\n\nMarathi transcript\n\n        \342\206\223\n\nTranslation Router\n\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Hindi\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Tamil\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Bengali\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Gujarati\n        \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Telugu\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 English\n\n        \342\206\223\n\nEach listener receives\ntheir selected language.\n```\n\n---\n\n# Important: Language Detection\n\nAllow the broadcaster to select the source language manually.\n\nAlso provide an optional:\n\n**Auto Detect Language**\n\nfeature.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nSource Language\n\n\342\227\213 Marathi\n\342\227\213 Hindi\n\342\227\213 English\n\342\227\217 Auto Detect\n```\n\nIf Auto Detect is enabled, the system should identify the spoken language where the underlying speech recognition provider supports reliable detection.\n\nManual selection should remain the recommended option for maximum accuracy.\n\n---\n\n# Indian Script Support\n\nThe UI must correctly render Indian scripts.\n\nTest the application with:\n\n```text\n\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\n\340\244\256\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\240\340\245\200\n\340\246\254\340\246\276\340\246\202\340\246\262\340\246\276\n\340\252\227\340\253\201\340\252\234\340\252\260\340\252\276\340\252\244\340\253\200\n\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\340\260\244\340\261\206\340\260\262\340\261\201\340\260\227\340\261\201\n\340\262\225\340\262\250\340\263\215\340\262\250\340\262\241\n\340\264\256\340\264\262\340\264\257\340\264\276\340\264\263\340\264\202\n\340\254\223\340\254\241\340\254\274\340\254\277\340\254\206\n\340\250\252\340\251\260\340\250\234\340\250\276\340\250\254\340\251\200\n\340\246\205\340\246\270\340\246\256\340\247\200\340\246\257\340\246\274\340\246\276\n\330\247\330\261\330\257\331\210\n\340\244\270\340\244\202\340\244\270\340\245\215\340\244\225\340\245\203\340\244\244\n\340\244\250\340\245\207\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\245\200\n\340\244\256\340\245\210\340\244\245\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\245\200\n\340\244\225\340\245\213\340\244\202\340\244\225\340\244\243\340\245\200\n\330\263\331\206\332\214\331\212\n\340\244\241\340\245\213\340\244\227\340\244\260\340\245\200\n\340\244\270\340\244\202\340\244\245\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\245\200\n\340\244\254\340\245\213\340\244\241\340\245\213\n\340\246\256\340\247\210\340\246\244\340\247\210\340\246\262\340\247\213\340\246\250\340\247\215\n\332\251\331\262\330\264\331\217\330\261\n```\n\nUse Unicode throughout the system.\n\nDo not assume Latin/English characters.\n\n---\n\n# RTL Language Support\n\nThe platform must support languages such as Urdu and Sindhi that may require right-to-left rendering.\n\nThe interface should dynamically switch text direction based on the selected language.\n\nExample:\n\n```typescript\ndirection = language.direction\n```\n\nFor RTL languages:\n\n```text\ndir=\"rtl\"\n```\n\nEnsure transcript, translated text, controls and typography remain usable.\n\n---\n\n# Indian Language Audio\n\nText-to-speech must also be language-aware.\n\nThe system should select an appropriate voice based on:\n\n```text\nlanguage\n+\nregion\n+\navailable voice\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nHindi \342\206\222 Hindi voice\nMarathi \342\206\222 Marathi voice\nTamil \342\206\222 Tamil voice\nBengali \342\206\222 Bengali voice\nTelugu \342\206\222 Telugu voice\n```\n\nDo not simply use an English voice to pronounce Indian-language text.\n\n---\n\n# Language Quality Layer\n\nCreate a provider capability system.\n\nNot every AI provider will have equal quality for every Indian language.\n\nTherefore maintain:\n\n```typescript\ninterface LanguageCapability {\n  languageCode: string;\n  speechToText: boolean;\n  translation: boolean;\n  textToSpeech: boolean;\n  qualityLevel: \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"experimental\";\n}\n```\n\nThe platform should know which services support which languages.\n\nIf a language does not have reliable TTS, allow:\n\n**Text-only translation**\n\ninstead of breaking the entire experience.\n\n---\n\n# Future Expansion\n\nThe architecture must allow adding:\n\n* More Indian regional languages\n* Dialects\n* Indian English\n* Hinglish\n* Regional accents\n* Code-mixed speech\n\nFuture examples:\n\n```text\nHinglish \342\206\222 Marathi\nMarathi + English \342\206\222 Hindi\nTamil + English \342\206\222 Telugu\nHindi + English \342\206\222 Bengali\n```\n\nDo not build the initial architecture in a way that assumes users speak only one pure language.\n\n---\n\n# Core Product Principle\n\nThe platform should ultimately work like:\n\n**Speak in ANY supported Indian language \342\206\222 listener chooses ANY supported Indian language \342\206\222 translation happens live.**\n\nThe user should never need to know which AI model or translation provider is being used.\n\nThe complexity belongs inside the platform.\n\nThe user experience should remain:\n\n```text\nI SPEAK\n   \342\206\223\nCHOOSE MY LANGUAGE\n\nI LISTEN\n   \342\206\223\nCHOOSE MY LANGUAGE\n\nLIVE TRANSLATION\n```\n\nThe long-term goal is to make the platform a **real-time language bridge for India**.\n"
    }
  }
}
