  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining India-Specific Platform**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining an India-first multilingual translation platform. I\'m focusing on the core languages. I\'m prioritizing support for the 22+ official Indian languages, along with English, as this will drive the platform\'s initial usability. I am considering different architectures to handle various input methods.\n\n\n**Refining Core Platform Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating any-to-any translation capabilities, alongside a real-time processing pipeline. Language configuration is being centralized for comprehensive metadata. The UI is being designed with a focus on ease of language selection and auto-detection, and scripts and RTL are being supported. I\'m also planning a language quality layer. Finally, the full-stack architecture is using a server-side component for API security, with an India-first accessible visual design.\n\n\n**Considering Multi-User Implementation**\n\nI\'m now contemplating multi-user aspects, but starting with a single-user \"speak-and-listen\" interface. The goal is to build a robust \"Translator\" interface to showcase the core any-to-any translation functionality from the beginning, building in expandability. I\'m focusing on real-time updates. I\'ll stick with Tailwind directly. I\'ve updated `metadata.json` with \"Indian Language Bridge\" and initialized `server.ts` with Gemini API integration.\n\n\n**Implementing Core Features**\n\nI\'ve just updated the `package.json` scripts, and I\'m now focusing on defining core types and data structures within `src/types.ts` and `src/languages.ts`. I am creating a central list of the 23 languages. I\'m building out the backend in `server.ts` with Gemini API integration. This includes endpoints for translation and language detection. I\'m considering using Web Speech API for real-time STT where possible, with Gemini for translation and server-side TTS. I will fallback on client-side text input. The frontend is taking shape with components for language selection, transcription, translation display, and speech synthesis.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 527393583
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
