  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Real-Time Translation**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the implications of `gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview` within the Gemini API. This model\'s real-time capabilities are directly applicable to the core \"Real-Time Processing\" need. This aligns well with the architecture of a web applet. It is a robust option that is very interesting.\n\n\n**Prioritizing API Implementation**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to a REST-based translation router, leveraging `gemini-3.6-flash`, prioritizing reliability for text-based pipelines, particularly given the user\'s STT requirement. I\'ll build a server-side API with `/api/translate` and `/api/detect` endpoints, along with client-side components for STT, TTS, language config, and a user interface. Project structure setup and dependency management is in progress.\n\n\n"
