    modified_response: "I have completed the development of **Bharat Bridge**, a high-performance real-time multilingual translation platform for India.\n\n### \360\237\214\237 Key Features\n- **Neural Matrix UI**: A sophisticated 3-column \"Immersive UI\" dashboard designed for high-throughput linguistic processing.\n- **Full Indian Spectrum**: Support for all 22 scheduled languages of India plus English, featuring native script rendering and Unicode compliance.\n- **Bi-Directional Translation**: Seamless routing between any language pair (e.g., Marathi \342\206\222 Tamil, Bengali \342\206\222 Hindi) without restriction.\n- **Live Pipeline**: Integrated Speech-to-Text (STT), Gemini-powered translation, and Text-to-Speech (TTS) for an end-to-end communication loop.\n- **Intelligence Layer**: Auto-detection capabilities for source languages and real-time confidence metrics.\n- **Linguistic Accessibility**: RTL support for languages like Urdu and Sindhi, paired with native-name selectors for non-English speakers.\n\n### \360\237\233\240\357\270\217 Technical Implementation\n- **Backend Architecture**: Express.js server utilizing the Gemini 1.5 Flash model for low-latency, context-aware translations across Indian dialects.\n- **Frontend Engine**: React 19 with Vite, featuring `motion` for fluid state transitions and `lucide-react` for technical iconography.\n- **Typography**: Paired **Inter** for high-density UI metadata with **Playfair Display** for elegant transcript rendering.\n- **Grid Layout**: A responsive 12-column grid system that scales from mobile handhelds to wide-screen desktop dashboards.\n\nThe platform is now ready to serve as a real-time linguistic bridge, connecting the diverse voices of India through a unified neural interface."
