  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have implemented the User Profile and Preferences feature for Bharat Bridge, enabling a personalized and efficient translation experience:\n\n### **Personalized User Profiles**\n- **Neural Bridge Defaults**: You can now set your preferred source and target languages within the **User Preferences** menu. These settings are persisted locally and will be automatically applied every time you return to the platform.\n- **Session Synchronization**: Changing your defaults in the settings menu now instantly updates your active translation session, providing a seamless transition between configuration and usage.\n\n### **Saved Translation Pairs**\n- **One-Click Saving**: A new **Star** icon has been integrated into the Neural Translation Bridge. You can instantly save your current language combination (e.g., Marathi to Hindi) for quick retrieval.\n- **Saved Configurations Grid**: A dedicated quick-access panel now displays your most frequently used language pairs. Switching between complex translation nodes is now as simple as a single click.\n- **Preference Management**: The User Preferences modal includes a management section where you can view your saved pairs and remove those you no longer need.\n\n### **Technical Implementation**\n- **Local Persistence**: Integrated a robust `localStorage` state engine to ensure your preferences survive browser restarts and session timeouts without requiring a backend account.\n- **Responsive Management**: Designed a high-contrast, themed `ProfileModal` using **Motion** for smooth transitions and **Lucide** icons for an intuitive management interface.\n- **State Synchronization**: Implemented complex state hooks to keep the user profile, active session languages, and the \"Saved Configurations\" grid perfectly synchronized."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
