  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Bharat Bridge Testing**\n\nI\'m focusing on Bharat Bridge testing, specifically the language selection feature. My initial thought is to outline the main features, and user interaction, which includes language selection. Next, I plan to break down potential user interactions and edge cases within that feature.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "To test **Bharat Bridge**, you can follow these steps to explore its real-time translation and profile features:\n\n### 1. Basic Text Translation\n*   **Select Languages**: Click on the **Source Selection** (left) and **Target Selection** (right) panels. Choose **English** as the source and **Hindi** or **Marathi** as the target.\n*   **Type Content**: Enter a sentence in the left textarea, for example: *\"Artificial Intelligence will transform India\'s future.\"*\n*   **Real-time Bridge**: You will see the center \"Neural Bridge\" pulse. After a brief pause, the translated text will appear in the right panel in the correct script.\n\n### 2. Speech-to-Text (STT) & Audio\n*   **Voice Input**: Click the **Mic** icon in the input panel. Grant microphone permission if prompted. Speak clearly in your source language. Your speech will be transcribed in real-time.\n*   **Listen**: Click the **Speaker** icon in the output panel to hear the translation spoken back in a native-sounding voice for that specific language.\n\n### 3. Auto-Detection\n*   **Toggle Auto-Detect**: Click the **AUTO DETECT** button in the source panel.\n*   **Test Detection**: Paste a sentence in any Indian language (e.g., *\"\340\244\206\340\244\234 \340\244\206\340\244\252\340\244\243 \340\244\250\340\244\265\340\245\200\340\244\250 \340\244\225\340\244\276\340\244\271\340\245\200\340\244\244\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\266\340\244\277\340\244\225\340\245\202\340\244\257\340\244\276\"*) without selecting the source language. The system will identify it as Marathi and translate it to your chosen target.\n\n### 4. User Profile & Saved Pairs\n*   **Set Defaults**: Click the **Settings (Gear)** icon in the header. Change your \"Default Source\" to Marathi and \"Default Target\" to Hindi. Close the modal; you\'ll notice the app immediately switches to these nodes.\n*   **Save a Pair**: While on a specific translation (e.g., Marathi \342\206\222 Tamil), click the **Star** icon in the center bridge. \n*   **Quick Access**: The saved pair will now appear in the **\"Saved Configurations\"** grid in the center column. You can tap it anytime to instantly switch back to that specific language mapping.\n\n### 5. RTL Layout Test\n*   **Switch to Urdu**: Select **Urdu** as the target language. Notice how the text alignment and direction automatically flip to **Right-to-Left (RTL)** to respect the script\'s requirements.\n\nYou can view the live app via the **Development App URL** in your preview window to begin testing these flows!"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 809731558
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
