  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Database Structure**\n\nI\'m currently deciding on the best database structure. I\'ve considered using a `sessions` collection with a `messages` subcollection. However, the requirement for an \"admin panel\" is causing me to rethink, so now I\'m debating a flat `messages` collection with a `sessionId` or if the subcollection is fine.\n\n\n**Refining Database Schema**\n\nI\'ve decided to proceed with the `sessions` collection and nested `messages` structure for real-time listener updates, although collection group queries were considered, it felt simpler. I\'ve switched to a \"Bridge Session\" approach, where the speaker creates a session, and listeners join. When the speaker speaks, messages are added to `sessions/{sessionId}/messages`, and listeners use `onSnapshot` on that subcollection.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
