  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully implemented the real-time translation bridge features, transforming Bharat Bridge into a live multi-user communication platform.\n\n### Core Enhancements:\n\n*   **Live Neural Bridge**:\n    *   **Live Broadcasts**: Speakers can now start a live session that broadcasts their speech and its translation in real-time.\n    *   **Interactive Listening**: Listeners can join active sessions using a session ID to receive instant transcriptions and translations.\n    *   **Real-time Sync**: Integrated **Firebase Firestore** to sync conversation data with a maximum 5-second latency, ensuring a seamless experience.\n*   **Data Persistence & Admin Panel**:\n    *   **Conversation Logs**: Every live session and its messages are automatically saved to Firestore, accessible to both the speaker and listener.\n    *   **Admin Dashboard**: A dedicated admin view (accessible via the user\'s email) allows for the oversight and review of all system sessions and message histories.\n*   **User Identity & Preferences**:\n    *   **Google Authentication**: Implemented secure sign-in to manage sessions and preferences across devices.\n    *   **Persistent Profiles**: Users can set default source/target languages and save frequently used translation pairs to their local profile.\n\n### Technical Implementation:\n- **Firebase Firestore**: Used for real-time document snapshots and hierarchical data storage (`sessions/{id}/messages`).\n- **Firebase Auth**: Integrated Google OAuth for user identification.\n- **Dynamic Translation Feed**: Updated the speech recognition engine to push interim and final results to the live cloud bridge during broadcasts.\n- **Security Hardening**: Implemented robust Firestore security rules to protect session data and enforce speaker-only write permissions.\n\nTo test the live feature, sign in, start a broadcast, copy the session ID, and open the app in a separate tab or device to join as a listener."
