  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Synthesizing Progress Report**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the Gemini Multimodal Live API (`gemini-3.5-live-translate-preview`) using WebSockets for real-time voice translation. Furthermore, I\'ve incorporated gender selection into the user profile, paving the way for a more personalized synthesized voice experience.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the requested enhancements for the Bharat Bridge application, focusing on real-time AI-powered translation and personalized voiceovers.\n\n### Key Implementation Details:\n\n-   **Gemini Live API Integration**: I integrated the **Gemini 3.5 Multimodal Live API** to handle low-latency, real-time voice translation. This replaces the previous polling-based method with a continuous WebSocket stream.\n-   **WebSocket Infrastructure**: A new WebSocket server has been implemented in `server.ts`. It manages communication rooms, allowing speakers to broadcast their translated voice and transcriptions to multiple listeners simultaneously.\n-   **Gender-Aware Voiceover**:\n    -   Added a **Gender Selection** toggle in the User Profile modal.\n    -   The system dynamically selects the translation voice based on the speaker\'s gender: using the **Fenrir** model for male voices and **Zephyr** for female voices, ensuring a natural and consistent listening experience for the listener.\n-   **High-Fidelity Audio Streaming**:\n    -   **Input**: Captures 16kHz PCM audio from the speaker\'s microphone.\n    -   **Output**: Plays back 24kHz PCM translated audio for the listener.\n    -   **Buffer Management**: Implemented precise audio scheduling to ensure gapless, low-latency playback (targeting $<5$ seconds delay).\n-   **Conversation Persistence**:\n    -   Every message in a live session is automatically saved to **Firestore**.\n    -   The **Admin Panel** has been updated to provide full visibility into all active and historical sessions, allowing for oversight of the \"Neural Bridge\" transmissions.\n-   **Full-Stack Architecture**: Updated the build system to be fully compliant with the platform\'s full-stack requirements, using `esbuild` to bundle the server-side logic securely.\n\n### How to use:\n1.  **Set Your Profile**: Open the profile modal to select your gender and default language nodes.\n2.  **Start a Live Bridge**: Click **\"Go Live\"** to start a session. Your voice will be streamed, translated, and broadcasted in real-time.\n3.  **Join a Session**: Listeners can enter a **Session ID** to join the bridge and hear the translation in the speaker\'s selected target language with the appropriate gendered voice."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 454623279
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
