    thinking: "**Implementing New Features**\n\nI\'ve integrated a unified portal using WebSockets and Gemini Live for real-time interaction. I\'ve also added gender selection in preferences, which dynamically changes the Gemini Live voice to Zephyr (female) or Fenrir (male), depending on user choice. Finally, I\'ve enabled comprehensive saving functionality.\n\n\n**Refining Access Control**\n\nI\'m now focusing on admin access and the listener experience. Admins can access all sessions and see both the original and translated transcripts, a key feature. Listeners receive real-time audio and both the speaker\'s original and translated text concurrently. I\'m also reviewing the audio-saving feasibility: saving raw audio chunks to Firestore appears inefficient, and I\'ll focus on storing transcripts instead, since this is the primary user request. I\'m also doing one final check to confirm that the server receives gender preference correctly. Finally, I need to verify that the specified Gemini model alias is correct.\n\n\n"
