  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have completed the requested features for Bharat Bridge, transforming it into a high-fidelity, real-time multilingual broadcast portal.\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n\n*   **Unified Live Portal**: A common interface for Speakers and Listeners. Users can start a **Live Broadcast** or join an existing one using a unique Session ID.\n*   **Real-time Neural Translation**: Powered by the **Gemini Multimodal Live API** and WebSockets, the app provides sub-second translation and transcription. \n    *   **Speakers** broadcast their voice directly through the browser.\n    *   **Listeners** receive high-quality translated audio and real-time text updates.\n*   **Intelligent Voice Synthesis**: \n    *   Users can now set their **Gender** (Male/Female) in the Preferences panel.\n    *   The system automatically adjusts the listener\'s voiceover to match the speaker\'s gender (using the **Fenrir** and **Zephyr** neural voices).\n*   **Comprehensive Session Persistence**: \n    *   Every live message is saved in **Firebase Cloud Firestore**.\n    *   The system logs four distinct data points for every transmission: the speaker\'s **original transcription**, the **translated text**, and metadata for both languages.\n*   **Admin Control Panel**: \n    *   A secure admin dashboard (accessible via the `Languages` icon for authorized users) allows for monitoring all active and past sessions.\n    *   Admins can view full conversation histories, including both original and translated transcripts.\n*   **User Preferences**: \n    *   Users can set default source/target languages and save frequently used pairs for quick access.\n    *   Preferences are persisted across sessions using local storage and verified via Firebase Auth.\n\n### Technical Overview:\n-   **Backend**: Node.js Express server with a WebSocket layer managing real-time room logic and Gemini Live connections.\n-   **Frontend**: React with Tailwind CSS, utilizing `AudioContext` for low-latency PCM audio playback and streaming.\n-   **Persistence**: Firestore for scalable, real-time message synchronization and Firebase Auth for secure user identity.\n\nYou can now test the live feature by opening the app in two windows: one as a **Speaker** (Broadcast) and one as a **Listener** (Join)."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
