  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Scaling the Bridge**\n\nI\'m evaluating the architecture for the \"Bharat Bridge\" app. My focus is on scaling live translation to accommodate over a thousand listeners for a national event. I\'m exploring the current WebSocket and Firestore setup. The WebSocket server (on Cloud Run/container) needs careful consideration to avoid reaching its limits under such load, though it could work well for broadcast scenarios.\n\n\n**Scaling Audio Transmission**\n\nI\'ve been concentrating on the audio transmission bottleneck for the 1000+ listener scenario. Broadcasting audio is the critical point. My thought is that while the standard Node.js WebSocket setup can handle the concurrent connections, the audio buffer distribution is the key. Firestore\'s limits appear manageable for the required read/write operations, although I\'ll keep an eye on the write rate. The UI needs to be optimized for a \"Broadcast Dashboard\" and \"Listener View\" layout.\n\n\n**Refining Broadcast Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on optimizing the `server.ts` broadcast logic. My main focus is on making it extremely robust for a high number of listeners, specifically with error handling for potential send failures. I\'m also adding a \"Share Session\" feature using a link, and adjusting the UI to match the scale of the event, aiming for a professional broadcast feel. I need to keep in mind that for this level of scale, the user may need a more involved setup.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will optimize the **Bharat Bridge** architecture for high-capacity broadcasting, enabling it to scale for 1000+ listeners by streamlining the WebSocket event loop and enhancing the \"Event Broadcast\" UI.\n\n### 1. Robust Broadcast Engine\nI\'ll update the server-side broadcast logic to handle large listener groups more efficiently, ensuring that audio and transcription packets are delivered with minimal latency even at scale.\n\n### 2. Event Dashboard\nI\'ll enhance the speaker UI with an \"Event Statistics\" view, showing real-time listener counts and connectivity status.\n\n### 3. Streamlined Access\nI\'ll implement a simple \"Join via ID\" system and a shareable session link to facilitate quick entry for hundreds of attendees.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Optimize Server Broadcast Logic\nI will modify `server.ts` to handle broadcasts more safely and efficiently.\n\n"
