    thinking: "**Adding Download Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating a `downloadTranscript` function and button into the live session UI within `App.tsx`. I\'ve located the approximate section for the UI, between lines 1028 and 1100 from a previous view file. I\'ll focus on implementing the download mechanism within this existing structure.\n\n\n**Refining Download Logic**\n\nI\'ve located the `messages` state definition at line 411, essential for accessing the transcript data. Now, the `downloadTranscript` function is taking shape within `App`. I\'m focusing on crafting a comprehensive text format, including session info and chronological message ordering, addressing the timestamp-based sorting. I am resolving the sorting issue and constructing the transcript content dynamically.\n\n\n**Implementing Download Function**\n\nI\'ve finalized the `downloadTranscript` function, now complete with session information and properly formatted, timestamp-sorted messages. I generated a downloadable text file using a Blob, URL, and a dynamically created `a` element for the download. I placed the function directly before the `return` statement in the `App` component. My focus now is on integrating a download button into the live session UI. I\'ve pinpointed the relevant section of the UI code between lines 1028 and 1044 where I can insert this button.\n\n\n**Positioning Download Button**\n\nI\'ve decided to incorporate the \"Download Transcript\" button adjacent to the \"End/Leave\" button within the live session UI for clarity. Furthermore, I\'ll add a corresponding button to the `AdminModal` to provide transcript download functionality from the admin interface, leveraging the existing `sessionMessages` state. I\'m prioritizing accessible placement and intuitive UI flow.\n\n\n**Enhancing Function Accessibility**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `exportTranscript` helper function, aiming for broad accessibility across components. I\'ve considered that the `AdminModal` and main UI components share the need for transcript download. This helper will take in message data and session details and generate the download file. I\'m prioritizing its use across components.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I\'ve updated the application to include a **Download Transcript** feature. You can now export the complete conversation history as a formatted text file from both live sessions and the session history panel.\n\n### Key Enhancements:\n- **Export Utility**: Added a robust transcript exporter that handles message sequencing, timestamps, and dual-language formatting.\n- **Live Session Integration**: Added a \"Download\" button to the active session header for both speakers and listeners.\n- **History Archival**: Added the ability to download transcripts from previous sessions via the Admin/History panel.\n- **Improved UI**: Integrated the download action using a clean icon-based button that fits the existing design system.\n\nThe exported file includes:\n- Session metadata (Name, ID, and Date).\n- Chronological message history.\n- Both the original and translated text for every entry.\n\n"
