  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Language Access**\n\nI\'m focusing on language accessibility in Bharat Bridge. My analysis of the existing code highlights the \'Speaker\' and \'Listener\' roles, and that audio is broadcast. I\'m exploring how to enable language selection for listeners, and how this could connect to the audio broadcast.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "To hear the speaker\'s live speech in your preferred language using **Bharat Bridge**, here is what you need to ensure and the steps you should follow:\n\n### 1. Pre-Join Checklist\n*   **Language Selection**: On the main screen, look for the **\"Your Language\"** setting. Click it to select the regional language you wish to hear (e.g., Hindi, Tamil, Bengali). The system will specifically translate the speaker\'s voice into this language for you.\n*   **Session ID**: Ensure you have the unique **Event ID** or **Invite Link** provided by the speaker/host.\n*   **Audio Output**: Make sure your device volume is turned up and you have a stable internet connection for a smooth audio stream.\n\n### 2. How to Join\n1.  Click on **Join Event (Listener Mode)**.\n2.  Enter the **Session ID** when prompted (or if you used an invite link, you will be joined automatically).\n3.  Once joined, the app establishes a secure \"Bridge\" to the live event.\n\n### 3. How You Will Hear the Speech\n*   **Real-time AI Translation**: As the speaker talks, their audio is sent to our AI server. The server processes the speech and translates it into your chosen language in milliseconds.\n*   **Live Audio Stream**: You will hear the translated speech played back through your device\'s speakers or headphones almost instantly.\n*   **Synchronized Transcription**: While you listen, the app will also display the **live transcription and translation** on your screen. This allows you to read along in your language if you miss a word.\n*   **Persistence**: All translations are saved to the session history. You can click the **Export** button at any time to download a full text transcript of everything said during the event.\n\n**Note for Listeners**: If you don\'t hear any audio immediately after joining, simply tap anywhere on the screen. Most browsers require a user interaction (like a click) before they allow an app to start playing live audio streams."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 658792168
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
