  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Testing Methodologies**\n\nI\'ve been considering how to best approach testing this application\'s speaker and listener functionality. I\'m leaning toward suggesting the use of separate tabs within a single browser, or, for more robust testing, separate devices. It also occurs to me that the \'Invite Link\' feature would be beneficial for the user in this situation.\n\n\n**Refining Testing Strategy**\n\nI\'ve crafted a comprehensive testing guide. It details step-by-step instructions for utilizing separate browser tabs, emphasizing the \"Invite Link\" for easy listener access. The guide covers speaker setup, invite link copying, listener joining, and language selection. I\'ll also suggest testing across separate devices, leveraging the shareable invite link. I\'ll double check the \"Invite Link\" is fully functional.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "You can test the multi-user experience right now in this application using **two browser tabs** on your computer, or by opening the link on your **phone**.\n\nHere is the easiest way to test it yourself:\n\n### 1. Set up the Speaker (Tab 1)\n1.  Open the application in your first tab.\n2.  Ensure your **Source Language** (e.g., English) is selected.\n3.  Click **Host Event (Speaker Mode)**.\n4.  Once the session is active, you will see an **Invite Link** button. Click it to copy the direct link to your clipboard.\n\n### 2. Set up the Listener (Tab 2)\n1.  Open a **new browser tab** and paste the Invite Link you just copied.\n2.  The application will automatically detect the session and ask you to join.\n3.  **Crucial Step**: In the listener tab, click on **\"Your Language\"** and select the language you want to hear (e.g., Hindi, Gujarati, Tamil).\n4.  The listener will now be waiting for audio.\n\n### 3. Start the Live Translation\n1.  Go back to **Tab 1 (Speaker)** and start speaking into your microphone.\n2.  Switch to **Tab 2 (Listener)**. You will:\n    *   **Hear** the translation in the language you chose.\n    *   **See** the transcription update in real-time.\n\n### Testing on Different Devices\nSince Bharat Bridge is a real-time platform, you can also send that **Invite Link** to a friend or open it on your mobile phone. As long as you are the \"Speaker\" on one device, any number of \"Listeners\" on other devices can join and hear you in their own preferred languages simultaneously.\n\n**Summary of Requirements for Listeners:**\n*   **Active Session**: The speaker must be \"Live\".\n*   **Language Preference**: Each listener must select their own target language to get the correct AI-generated voice.\n*   **Unmute**: Most browsers require you to interact with the page (click anywhere) before they allow audio to play automatically."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 926873244
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
