    modified_response: "To test the **Bharat Bridge** application as both a Speaker and a Listener, you can use the link below. You can open this link in multiple tabs or different devices.\n\n### Your Application Link\n**[Open Bharat Bridge in a New Tab](https://ais-pre-5emmrrifmlalmysuxgi2yo-798786346053.asia-east1.run.app)**\n\n---\n\n### How to Test (Speaker & Listener)\nTo simulate a live event right now on your computer, follow these steps:\n\n1.  **Start as the Speaker:**\n    *   Open the link above in your main browser window.\n    *   Click **\"Host Event\"** (Speaker Mode).\n    *   Once the session starts, look for the **\"Invite Link\"** or **\"Session ID\"** at the top. Click it to copy the link.\n    *   Ensure your microphone is active.\n\n2.  **Join as a Listener:**\n    *   Open a **new tab** or, ideally, an **Incognito/Private window** (this allows you to act as a different user).\n    *   Paste the **Invite Link** you copied, or go to the app home and click **\"Join Event\"** and enter the Session ID.\n    *   **Crucial Step:** Before joining, select a different **\"Your Language\"** (e.g., Hindi, Tamil, or French) to hear the translation.\n\n3.  **The Live Experience:**\n    *   Speak into the \"Speaker\" tab.\n    *   In the \"Listener\" tab, you will see the **Live Transcription** appearing in your chosen language.\n    *   You will also **hear the translated audio** played back in that language in real-time.\n\n### Tips for Testing:\n*   **Use Headphones:** If you are testing on one computer, use headphones to avoid audio feedback loops where the speaker\'s microphone picks up the listener\'s translated audio.\n*   **Incognito Mode:** Using an Incognito window for the listener is the best way to ensure the two tabs don\'t \"share\" the same user login, allowing you to see exactly what a separate user would see."
