  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Direct Application Links**\n\nI\'m focusing on the user\'s issue with the live application link. It seems they\'re hitting a \"Redirect Notice\" from Google, a common pitfall. To combat this, I\'m prioritizing providing direct application URLs for clarity and a seamless experience. My aim is to circumvent any potential environmental link challenges.\n\n\n**Addressing Testing Procedures**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears to address the user\'s testing procedure, given the context of the redirect notice. My initial thought was server-side issues and build verification, but the screenshot clarifies Google\'s redirect mechanism, and thus the user simply needs to click on that \"Redirect Notice\" link. I need to guide the user to test the correct links provided earlier.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "To test your application as both a **Speaker** and a **Listener** at the same time, you can follow these steps:\n\n### 1. Access the Application\nThe \"Redirect Notice\" you\'re seeing is a standard security screen from Google. You simply need to click the blue link on that page (the one starting with `https://ais-pre...`) to proceed to your live app.\n\n**Direct Links:**\n*   **Primary URL:** [Click here to open Bharat Bridge](https://ais-pre-5emmrrifmlalmysuxgi2yo-798786346053.asia-east1.run.app)\n*   **Development URL:** [Click here for the Dev version](https://ais-dev-5emmrrifmlalmysuxgi2yo-798786346053.asia-east1.run.app)\n\n### 2. How to Test with Two Users\nYou do **not** need two separate devices. You can test it entirely on your current computer using two browser tabs:\n\n1.  **Tab 1 (The Speaker):**\n    *   Open the link above.\n    *   Click **\"Host Event\"** (Speaker Mode).\n    *   Once the session starts, look for the **Session ID** (usually displayed at the top or in the stats).\n    *   Start speaking. Your audio will be sent to the server for translation.\n\n2.  **Tab 2 (The Listener):**\n    *   Open the same link in a **new tab** or an **Incognito/Private window**.\n    *   Click **\"Join Event\"** (Listener Mode).\n    *   Enter the **Session ID** from Tab 1.\n    *   Select your **Target Language** (e.g., Hindi, Tamil, etc.).\n    *   You will now hear the translated audio and see the live transcriptions coming from the Speaker in Tab 1.\n\n### 3. What to Ensure\n*   **Microphone Permissions:** Ensure you allow microphone access in the Speaker tab.\n*   **Audio Output:** Make sure your volume is up on the Listener tab to hear the translations.\n*   **Incognito Mode (Optional):** Using an Incognito window for the second tab is a great way to ensure the two \"users\" have completely separate sessions.\n\nBy using two tabs, you can immediately verify that the translation bridge is working across different languages!"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 81908993
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
